<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!-- DESIGN LEDGER
XLeRobot platform for alternate arms: controller_manager, MuJoCo, RSP, RViz.
Units m, kg, s, rad; REP-103 +X forward +Y left +Z up. Root base_footprint;
base_link is the chassis, nominal height 0.035 m, initial world heading removed
by the odometry bridge. Body, wheel/head joint frames, mesh scales, limits,
inertias and white cart finish copied from the canonical standard xlerobot.urdf.
Source XLeRobot b017b5e6354bd9f61f4247a920c72622ca0aade0; source robot assets
retained via meshes/ and full_meshes/. No SO arm subtrees or SO base-holder visuals.
arm_mount_L/R are frame-only mounting datums inherited from the corrected
cart assembly; Mod101 mount brackets/bolt alignment need hardware verification.
Cart/head assembly Z correction -0.0359257260090011 m follows source caster
bounds and omniwheel radius. The 8 kg cart box estimate and computed inertia
include caster mass redistributed in MuJoCo. Internal caster and roller joints
are omitted from ROS; caster visuals retain nominal pose. Connector meshes
from pinned upstream hardware, with mesh-derived Z fit, XY motor-mount fit.
Visual-only fixed frames omit inertials. MJCF owns platform collision geometry.
Head RGB-D pinhole/optical frames and provisional bottom IMU copied unchanged.
This explicit platform URDF is included by the Mod101 Xacro configuration;
that profile adds arms and the single SimulatorSystem ros2_control block.
-->
<robot name="xlerobot">
